---
import SignalLayout from '../../layouts/SignalLayout.astro';
import ComparisonTable from '../../components/ComparisonTable.astro';
import '../../styles/comparisons.css';
---

<SignalLayout title="YouTube client alternatives | OpenTubeX" description="Compare desktop and mobile YouTube clients by privacy, data import, sync, downloads, and tabs. Each table entry links to a source where possible." active="compare">
	<main class="resource-page comparison-page">
		<header class="page-hero">
			<div class="page-hero__content">
				<p class="page-hero__eyebrow">Client comparison</p>
				<h1 class="page-hero__title">Compare YouTube clients</h1>
				<p class="page-hero__lede">This table compares OpenTubeX with FreeTube, Grayjay, NewPipe, LibreTube, and YouTube. It covers platforms, privacy, playback, and library tools for people looking at FreeTube alternatives.</p>
			</div>
		</header>
		<section class="section section--page comparison-results" aria-labelledby="comparison-results-heading">
			<h2 class="section__title" id="comparison-results-heading">What each client supports</h2>
			<ComparisonTable />
			<p class="comparison-note">Maintained by OpenTubeX. Sources checked <time datetime="2026-10-01">1 October 2026</time>. Support can vary by release and platform.</p>
		</section>
		<section class="section section--page comparison-guide" aria-labelledby="comparison-guide-heading">
			<h2 class="section__title" id="comparison-guide-heading">What to check before switching</h2>
			<div class="comparison-guide__grid">
				<article id="import">
					<h3>Move your library</h3>
					<p>OpenTubeX imports FreeTube <code>.db</code> data for subscriptions, watch history, search history, and playlists. Export the database from FreeTube, then use the matching import actions in OpenTubeX. Copy downloaded files separately; open tabs do not transfer.</p>
					<p><a href="/docs/importing/#move-from-another-app">Import instructions</a></p>
				</article>
				<article id="sync">
					<h3>Use more than one device</h3>
					<p>FreeTube's official app runs on desktop and stores data locally. OpenTubeX runs on desktop and Android, with an experimental iOS/iPadOS app. Its optional sync uses end-to-end encryption to protect selected data before upload.</p>
					<p><a href="/docs/sync/">OpenTubeX sync guide</a> · <a href="https://docs.freetubeapp.io/usage/data-location/">FreeTube data storage</a></p>
				</article>
				<article id="offline-downloads">
					<h3>Offline downloads</h3>
					<p>FreeTube removed its built-in downloader in version 0.24.0 and recommends separate download tools. OpenTubeX supports video, audio, playlist, and available subtitle downloads. File formats and quality depend on the video and platform.</p>
					<p><a href="/docs/downloads/">OpenTubeX download guide</a> · <a href="https://github.com/FreeTubeApp/FreeTube/releases/tag/v0.24.0-beta">FreeTube 0.24.0 release notes</a></p>
				</article>
				<article id="tabs">
					<h3>Tabs and windows</h3>
					<p>FreeTube supports separate windows but has no browser-style tabs. OpenTubeX keeps videos and channels open in tabs within the app. Its tab organizer lets you find an open tab.</p>
					<p><a href="/extra-features/#tab-support">OpenTubeX tab controls</a> · <a href="https://github.com/FreeTubeApp/FreeTube/issues/333">FreeTube tabs discussion</a></p>
				</article>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</SignalLayout>
